{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018RheEnXxsSckRHCh8Sj5Qm","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Filter out territories (PR and VI) and sum farmers markets\n# Territories to exclude: Puerto Rico (PR), Virgin Islands (VI)\nfact_filtered = fact.filter(\n    (fact.state_abbr != 'PR') & (fact.state_abbr != 'VI')\n)\nfact_totals = fact_filtered.aggregate(\n    total_farmers_markets=fact_filtered.farmers_markets.sum()\n).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nref_us = ref.filter(ref.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025').mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and compute rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fact_totals.join(ref_us, fact_totals.k == ref_us.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=fact_totals.total_farmers_markets / ref_us.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see the data. The territories are:\n- Puerto Rico (PR)\n- Virgin Islands (VI)\n\nThe 50 states plus DC are the \"U.S.\" excluding territories. So I need to sum all farmers markets EXCEPT Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands.\n\nNow let me create a build script that:\n1. Reads the farmers markets data\n2. Reads the census population data\n3. Filters out territories (PR and VI)\n4. Sums the farmers markets from the remaining states\n5. Gets the U.S. population from the census data\n6. Calculates the rate per 100,000\n\nThe challenge is that these are two different tables. According to the xorq-catalog skill, when you need a value from two datasets, you should:\n1. Read both sources\n2. Join them (using a constant key if needed since we're getting a single total)\n\nLet me create this script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018RheEnXxsSckRHCh8Sj5Qm","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Filter out territories (PR and VI) and sum farmers markets\n# Territories to exclude: Puerto Rico (PR), Virgin Islands (VI)\nfact_filtered = fact.filter(\n    (fact.state_abbr != 'PR') & (fact.state_abbr != 'VI')\n)\nfact_totals = fact_filtered.aggregate(\n    total_farmers_markets=fact_filtered.farmers_markets.sum()\n).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nref_us = ref.filter(ref.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025').mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and compute rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fact_totals.join(ref_us, fact_totals.k == ref_us.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=fact_totals.total_farmers_markets / ref_us.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":828,"cacheRead":17902,"cacheWrite":594,"totalTokens":19337,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0041400000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0017902000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.0007425,"total":0.006685700000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":211},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911594871,"responseId":"msg_011Ce73hYsfyhSn6RNYQ57sA","rawStopReason":"tool_use"}}
